From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 13:47:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: throttle Lara calls to stay under its per-second rate
 limit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Confirmed with Lara support: the "exceeded quota" 429 is a momentary
per-second character rate limit (1,000 chars/sec on Free, 10,000/sec
on paid plans), completely separate from the monthly character pool —
explains why it kept firing with the account nowhere near its monthly
usage. Several batched Lara calls (one per experience/section-group/
fact-group, run with bounded concurrency) could still burst past that
per-second ceiling when they landed in the same instant.

translateFields() (the single choke point every Lara call already goes
through) now:
- Reserves a character budget from a 1-second sliding window before
  each real call, queueing execution rather than firing immediately —
  applies automatically to every caller (experiences, enhancements,
  hero titles, proposal summary, site_copy seed script).
- Retries up to 2 more times with backoff specifically on rate-limit-
  shaped errors (429 / "quota" in the message), since Lara support
  confirmed this class of error is transient, not a hard stop.

